A||N||7||artherd||Classic Car insurance?||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||08-01-2001||05:03 AM||||I was wondering if anyone had any tips on an *alternative* sort of insurance for my 88?<P>I live in the People's Republic of California, and have State Farm now (they create a negative pressure differential...)<P>I'd like to stop paying out the nose, and since I drive the car less than 5k a year anyway (work at home.) It just makes sense.<P>Problem is, I don't know who to call, or what kind of coverage I get with what restrictions.<P>I know in general that this may be something I want to do, but no specifics.  <P>Can anyone out there more seasoned in these matters help me? <P>Thanks!<BR>Ben.<P> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Oreif||08-01-2001||12:48 PM||||I have mine insured as a "Classic Showcar" I have regular plates and can drive it up to 3400 miles per year. The car is insured for it's appraised value and the insurance is less expensive. I have my insurance thru Nationwide Insurance. In my state it also exempt's you from emission testing too!<BR>The important thing I was looking for was insured for appraised value. Most insurance companies insure it for wholesale value. This means if some idiot hits the rear bumper they could "total" the car. I have spent way too much money and time to have it totaled and only given a couple of grand for it. Some call it "showcar" or "pleasure vehicle". Usually there is restictions on amount of miles per year. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||08-01-2001||01:23 PM||||Check out Rally insurance Inc. they have basically the same deal as Oreif has but they<BR>can give you as much as 5,000 miles a year,<BR>which might be better with your nice year round climate.<BR>Look for Elite Collector Program of North America.<P>Rally: <A HREF="http://www.rallyinsurance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rallyinsurance.com</A> <P>BTW you must have another car to drive as a daily driver or "primary car".<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||4
Z||000003||fierobaby||08-01-2001||01:28 PM||||somehow I manage to have cheap insurence... Its only $245 every 6 months... I'm a teenager a female and I own a collectors sports car... my brother pays more on just his escort!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||08-02-2001||04:25 AM||||Hi all, thanks for the recomendations.  If I could exempt from emmisions testing (of my MUCH cleaner 98 Northstar, but hey) that would be a godsend. Then I wouldn't have to keep a v6 on a cradle and swap it in every two years :(<P>Connie: you lucky female you :)  I'm a 20 year old male with a spotless record, yet I pay almost four times what you pay.  (that does include "collision" coverage with $500 deductable though...)<P>Pretty big chunk of change to swallow, I would rather put it into the car!<P>(and I only drive ~5k/year anyway :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||08-02-2001||01:12 PM||||WOW. I pay $720 a year...or about $370 US. My Fiero is insured for $25,000 for that price. That is also unlimited KMS, but must not use the car for work purposes. As in driving to and from a job. As if I have one of them to go to though. On the other hand though after looking at FieroBabys brake problems in her sell her car thread, and only $200. Cool I thought. It cost me $1200 to do my brakes up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-02-2001||01:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>...female...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The operative word. <P>Having testosterone in your veins causes your insurance costs to at least double.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||6
